Requirements:
- Generate a valid YAML playbook, conforming to yamllint and ansible-lint.
- Follow the original task names and order exactly.
- Only fix issues reported in the error logs; do not alter the functional intent or add/remove tasks.
- Output must consist solely of the corrected YAML playbook.

Inputs:
- Original generation prompt: 
Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.  
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).  
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Check the current version of Docker Compose installed on the system.  
Description Task 1: Run the Docker Compose command with the version flag to capture the current version installed, ensuring no changes are made to the system during this check.

Task 2: Set a fact for the current Docker Compose version if it is defined and the output is not empty.  
Description Task 2: Extract the version number from the output of the Docker Compose version command and store it in a variable for later comparison.

Task 3: Delete the existing Docker Compose binary if the installed version does not match the desired version.  
Description Task 3: Remove the current Docker Compose binary if the extracted version does not match the specified version, ensuring no leading 'v' in the version string.

Task 4: Download and install the specified version of Docker Compose if it is not already installed or if the installed version is older.  
Description Task 4: Use the `get_url` module to download Docker Compose from a specified URL and place it in the desired location, setting the appropriate permissions, only if the current version is not defined, is empty, or is older than the required version.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Check the current version of Docker Compose installed on the system
  command: docker-compose --version
  register: docker_compose_version_check
  changed_when: false

- name: Set a fact for the current Docker Compose version if it is defined and the output is not empty
  set_fact:
    current_docker_compose_version: "{{ docker_compose_version_check.stdout | regex_search('docker-compose\\s*(\\S+)', '\\1') | first }}"
  when: docker_compose_version_check.stdout != ""

- name: Delete the existing Docker Compose binary if the installed version does not match the desired version
  file:
    path: /usr/local/bin/docker-compose
    state: absent
  when: current_docker_compose_version is defined and current_docker_compose_version != desired_version | string

- name: Download and install the specified version of Docker Compose if it is not already installed or if the installed version is older
  get_url:
    url: "https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/download/{{ desired_version }}/docker-compose-{{ ansible_system | lower }}-{{ ansible_machine }}"
    dest: /usr/local/bin/docker-compose
    mode: '0755'
  when: current_docker_compose_version is not defined or current_docker_compose_version == '' or current_docker_compose_version < desired_version


