n  ansible.builtin.pip:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: "{{ item_state }}"\n    version: "{{ item_version }}"\n    executable: "{{ python_pip_executable }}"\n  loop: "{{ python_pip_modules }}"\n  when:\n    - ansible_distribution_release not in [\'bookworm\', \'noble\']\n    - ansible_os_family != \'Alpine\'\n```\n\nThis playbook corrects the Fully Qualified Collection Names (FQCN) for Ansible modules, ensuring that the playbook will pass `ansible-lint`. The `rename` module was changed to `ansible.builtin.rename` as the `rename` module is deprecated and this is the correct FQCN to use for renaming files. The other tasks were updated to use `ansible.builtin.` prefix, adhering to the latest Ansible standards.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-14T22:12:05.631946135Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13898750345, 'load_duration': 72585244, 'prompt_eval_count': 3296, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1789082831, 'eval_count': 694, 'eval_duration': 12035548728, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--bbded202-ce53-4ef9-8d09-ba5c25af60c8-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3296, 'output_tokens': 694, 'total_tokens': 3990}
