content='```yaml\n---\n- name: Obtain the installed version of Python 3 on Debian 12\n  ansible.builtin.command: python3 --version\n  register: python_version_output\n  changed_when: false\n  tags: \n    - skip_ansible_lint\n    - molecule-idempotence-notest\n  when: ansible_facts[\'os_family\'] == \'Debian\' and ansible_facts[\'distribution_major_version\'] == \'12\'\n\n- name: Remove the EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file for Python 3.11 installations on Debian 12\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /usr/lib/python3.11/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    state: absent\n  when: "\'Python 3.11\' in python_version_output.stdout"\n  tags: \n    - skip_ansible_lint\n    - molecule-idempotence-notest\n```\n\nThis playbook is designed to be included directly in an Ansible Role under the `tasks/` directory, such as `tasks/main.yml`. It adheres to the specified instructions, ensuring that it can be used to manage Python 3 installations on Debian 12 systems. The playbook includes two tasks: one to check the installed Python 3 version and another to conditionally remove a specific file if Python 3.11 is detected. Both tasks are tagged to be excluded from testing with Molecule, as per the requirements.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-14T22:13:51.877907313Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 4196001663, 'load_duration': 60415752, 'prompt_eval_count': 422, 'prompt_eval_duration': 45176976, 'eval_count': 290, 'eval_duration': 4089128131, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--b6be46d9-4ad7-4c4f-8799-5af6e13068ba-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 422, 'output_tokens': 290, 'total_tokens': 712}
