content='```yaml\n---\n- name: Determine the package state based on the installation method\n  set_fact:\n    ansible_package_state: "{{ \'present\' if ansible_facts.packages[ansible_package_name] is defined else \'absent\' }}"\n\n- name: Setup Ansible on RedHat systems, excluding Fedora, using the package manager\n  include_tasks: redhat.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_os_family == \'RedHat\'\n    - ansible_distribution != \'Fedora\'\n    - ansible_package_state == \'present\'\n\n- name: Setup Ansible on Fedora using the package manager\n  include_tasks: fedora.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_os_family == \'RedHat\'\n    - ansible_distribution == \'Fedora\'\n    - ansible_package_state == \'present\'\n\n- name: Setup Ansible on Ubuntu using the package manager\n  include_tasks: ubuntu.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_os_family == \'Debian\'\n    - ansible_distribution == \'Ubuntu\'\n    - ansible_package_state == \'present\'\n\n- name: Setup Ansible on Debian using the package manager\n  include_tasks: debian.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_os_family == \'Debian\'\n    - ansible_distribution != \'Ubuntu\'\n    - ansible_package_state == \'present\'\n\n- name: Setup Ansible using Pip\n  include_tasks: pip.yml\n  when: ansible_package_state == \'absent\'\n```\n\nThis playbook structure adheres to the instructions provided, using `include_tasks` to manage separate tasks for different distributions and package managers. The conditions ensure the correct tasks are executed based on the OS and installation method.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-14T23:19:53.094842302Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 6235289258, 'load_duration': 58940925, 'prompt_eval_count': 486, 'prompt_eval_duration': 52557410, 'eval_count': 332, 'eval_duration': 6123139146, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--f3e648e9-3b3c-4350-a643-19d92b38a768-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 486, 'output_tokens': 332, 'total_tokens': 818}
_______________________________________Cleaned LLM Output:_______________________________________ 
---
- name: Determine the package state based on the installation method
  set_fact:
    ansible_package_state: "{{ 'present' if ansible_facts.packages[ansible_package_name] is defined else 'absent' }}"

- name: Setup Ansible on RedHat systems, excluding Fedora, using the package manager
  include_tasks: redhat.yml
  when:
    - ansible_os_family == 'RedHat'
    - ansible_distribution != 'Fedora'
    - ansible_package_state == 'present'

- name: Setup Ansible on Fedora using the package manager
  include_tasks: fedora.yml
  when:
    - ansible_os_family == 'RedHat'
    - ansible_distribution == 'Fedora'
    - ansible_package_state == 'present'

- name: Setup Ansible on Ubuntu using the package manager
  include_tasks: ubuntu.yml
  when:
    - ansible_os_family == 'Debian'
    - ansible_distribution == 'Ubuntu'
    - ansible_package_state == 'present'

- name: Setup Ansible on Debian using the package manager
  include_tasks: debian.yml
  when:
    - ansible_os_family == 'Debian'
    - ansible_distribution != 'Ubuntu'
    - ansible_package_state == 'present'

- name: Setup Ansible using Pip
  include_tasks: pip.yml
  when: ansible_package_state == 'absent'


